WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.359
&gt;&gt;&gt; After 20 years in power, Turkey's long-time
leader is facing a runoff election.

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:09.190
It could have huge implications for the nato
alliance and the war on Ukraine.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.190
This morning.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:28.270
It looks like Turkish president erdogan has
failed to maintain a majority.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:33.190
And he continues to block Sweden from joining
nato, which would be a huge blow to Vladimir

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.190
Putin.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:40.570
No one better to talk to this than CNN's international
correspondent Christiane Amanpour.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:48.351
Two years and a very complex relationship
between erdogan and Turkey and nato and the

00:00:48.351 --> 00:00:51.750
united States, because they prove critical
in some ways, the grand deal, et cetera.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.750
[8:07:31 AM]

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:53.750
deal, et cetera.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.329
But also, they prove to be very difficult.

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:56.770
&gt;&gt; They're difficult.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:01.449
Turkey is a difficult ally, because as you
pointed out, it's so important.

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:06.750
Nato has so many countries, but Turkey is
the second biggest military.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.799
And there, it's on the ground.

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:10.240
It's easily deployable.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:16.090
But over the years, Turkey has, particularly
under erdogan, starting about 20 years ago,

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:29.340
when he actually opened up and demo democratized
Turkey, then with the attempted coup against

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:35.549
him, he cracked down and started to become
a lot more authoritarian and that's what's

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:41.799
made him incredibly unpredictable when it
comes to being a rock-solid western ally.

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:47.939
And of course, before, Turkey used to be kind
of the de facto bridge between east and west.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:53.060
But under erdogan, they have dropped their
attempts to get into the eu, because there

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.060
are a lot of conditions that they are

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.060
[8:08:31 AM]

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.270
lot of conditions that they are unwilling
to meet.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.369
&gt;&gt; What does it say to you that this is going
to a runoff.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:03.361
That he couldn't get 50% of the vote and the
referendum of him that that is?

00:02:03.361 --> 00:02:05.250
&gt;&gt; It is a referendum.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:09.780
He is -- you know, he actually went into this
for the first time lagging in the votes.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:15.500
Now, what you've seen is, the vote count has
shown that he actually took more of the vote

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:20.430
in the first round than his challenger and
the challenger is, you know, part of a coalition.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.870
They banded together to see if they could,
in fact, unseat him.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.390
&gt;&gt; But it's never before worked?

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.820
&gt;&gt; Not in this way, no.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.379
Now it looks as if the election committee
has said, he's got more.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:32.730
He has 49 plus percent.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.410
He has not made it across the finish line
yet.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:43.550
To be fair, the Turkish system has never had
a runoff, it has only since 2018.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.010
He won handedly the first time.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.420
You can't say it's the first time in 20 years
that he's faced runoff, but the first time

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.420
since

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.420
[8:09:32 AM]

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.750
runoff, but the first time since they've had
a runoff that he's faced a runoff.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:03:05.760
A lot of people are learning the name Kamal
clich drulio.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.970
Is any struggle necessary?

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.580
People should be confident that we will definitely
win.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.480
But what he has put forward is such a contrast
to erdogan.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.670
He talked about the price of onions, filmed
this video in his modest kitchen.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.740
Trying to say, I'm so different from your
current president.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:27.780
&gt;&gt; And touching on the thing that's motivated
most voters, the cost of living crisis.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.790
The economic crisis is very, very severe.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:35.750
If you look at any reports that are coming
out of there, lots of interviews by ordinary

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:38.630
people who have to make a living and who have
to eat.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:42.760
Many people who have been voting akp, which
is erdogan's party for years, and he has a

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:49.360
very strong base, are saying, look, you know,
we are doing worse off than our families did

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.600
all of these years ago.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:54.420
We who used to eat chicken or meat once a
week are now maybe doing it once a month.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.420
[8:10:32 AM]

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.420
doing it once a month.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:02.130
So that on top of the earthquake, which killed
some 50 50,000 people and highlighted the

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:08.599
corruption that they have blamed the Turkish
government, allowing builders and others to

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:16.310
pay people under the table and have shoddy
construction, but he's a very good and canny

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.959
politician, this erdogan.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:20.799
And he knows and he has a very fervent base.

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:21.979
He is a politician.

00:04:21.979 --> 00:04:23.710
He used to be mayor of istanbul.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.500
He knows what it means to be a politician.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:27.990
The other gentlemen was an economist.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:32.509
He knows exactly what has to be done to get
the economy back on track, which is what people

00:04:32.509 --> 00:04:33.509
need.

00:04:33.509 --> 00:04:38.100
But some people have said his -- so far, anyway,
his campaign style has not matched that of

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.100
erdogan.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.100
We'll see.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.370
&gt;&gt; And the reason the complications for this
are so profound, of course, go Ukraine, at

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.370
the heart of that.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.370
&gt;&gt; At the moment.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.680
&gt;&gt; The other thing we saw over the weekend,
this development that was striking to me was

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.210
the prigozhin, the mers their chief of the
Wagner group that has been helping Russia

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.949
fight in Ukraine, back in January he

00:04:55.949 --> 00:04:56.949
[8:11:34 AM]

00:04:56.949 --> 00:05:00.700
Ukraine, back in January he offered to Ukrainian
intelligence service the position of Russian

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.700
troops.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:07.100
Basically, they would have the intent of firing
upon them, offering their positions if Ukraine

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:11.480
withdrew their soldiers from that key city
of bakhmut which has faced such intense fighting.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.520
What was your reaction from you?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:20.220
&gt;&gt; Look, is it absolutely really an intense
situation, because what prigozhin is doing

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:25.600
with his Wagner group is challenging Putin
without challenging Putin.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.120
He never attacks Putin himself.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:33.880
But he's constantly attacking, you know, the
two major military -- the defense minister

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.740
and the army commander.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:41.180
And he's trying to put himself in a good position
with Putin.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:44.350
And he has the only troops that apparently
are willing to go there.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.810
But you've seen that it actually hasn't worked
yet.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:50.770
I mean, they've tried and they've tried and
they've tried.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:52.970
And they have not achieved success in bakhmut.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.920
And it is a terrible meat grinder there.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.280
But the forces who are achieving slightly
more success right now

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.280
[8:12:36 AM]

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:02.509
slightly more success right now are the Ukrainian
troops.

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:06.699
And you know zelenskyy's in London today --
&gt;&gt; I was just going to ask you about that.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:13.120
&gt;&gt; He's been on a weekend tour of eu and allied
nato capitals saying, if you want us to go

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:17.849
on this counteroffensive, we need more help,
and we need the weapons you've been promising

00:06:17.849 --> 00:06:18.849
and we need more.

00:06:18.849 --> 00:06:20.960
And the British have been quite forward leaning.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:26.360
They have said that they want to and they're
ready to provide the much-longer range missiles

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.920
that the Americans have so far not wanted
to provide.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:33.090
&gt;&gt; And German, also, which is -- not giving
them so much money.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:39.940
&gt;&gt; You know, if the nato strategy and the
U.S. Strategy is for Putin to lose, then they

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:45.660
have to enable Ukraine to win.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:52.069
The ballots are still being counted for Turkey's
most consequential presidential election in

00:06:52.069 --> 00:06:55.259
decades, which appears to be headed for a
runoff.

00:06:55.259 --> 00:06:59.379
Preliminary results show recep tayyip erdogan,
the increasingly authoritarian leader who

00:06:59.379 --> 00:07:05.800
will the country for 20 years is a leading
but it's just below the 50% threshold needed

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:12.090
to secure the ballot, not an outright victory,
kemal kilicdaroglu joins me live in its angle.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.530
This probably is going to a runoff.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:18.179
Where does that leave the two contenders here?

00:07:18.179 --> 00:07:22.319
&gt;&gt; Well, you know, that is what it looks like
this morning, max.

00:07:22.319 --> 00:07:28.360
The electoral board saying they counted more
than 99% of the ballots which were cast.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:32.520
So far, they have president erdogan at 49.40%.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:40.530
Then followed by kemal kilicdaroglu, the opposition
candidate, 44.96%.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:43.410
So the most likely scenario here, will be
neither of them,

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.410
[8:01:26 AM]

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:45.849
here, will be neither of them, especially
if you look at the numbers from president

00:07:45.849 --> 00:07:51.169
erdogan, not achieving that 50 plus one required
to win the presidency.

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:56.120
Most likely it is headed to a runoff in about
two weeks time on may 28th.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.300
Then we heard from both sides saying that
they are ready for this.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.580
The opposition, just a short time ago.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:08.139
The main opposition party, the chp coming
out and saying they aren't ready for this

00:08:08.139 --> 00:08:12.320
runoff as we heard from their leader yesterday
as well, this is the will of the Turkish people.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:18.810
They are ready for this but also, they are
trying to continue to sound hopeful and optimistic.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:24.930
But no doubt, max, this has been a big blow
for an opposition that for the first time,

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:32.159
came together under this unified banner, a
coalition of the people, that they were presenting

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:37.760
one candidate to try and unseat president
erdogan.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:42.969
And really it was this feeling, that they
might have this chance of doing so.

00:08:42.969 --> 00:08:43.969
[8:02:26 AM]

00:08:43.969 --> 00:08:44.969
chance of doing so.

00:08:44.969 --> 00:08:45.980
They were promising people change.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:51.589
They were promising to take this country back
to being a real democracy, to reverse the

00:08:51.589 --> 00:08:54.370
years of president erdogan's rule.

00:08:54.370 --> 00:09:00.490
You had a lot of people who were really optimistic
about this coalition, seeing them unified,

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:03.420
seeing them were galvanized and other.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:08.060
Right now, a lot of people are disappointed,
and on the other side, you have president

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.310
erdogan, who is not used to losing.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:16.350
20 plus years of being at the top.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:22.800
While he is not secure that 50%, while this
is a likely scenario where it is headed towards

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:27.770
a runoff, again, they are still counting the
rest of the ballots.

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.930
This from president erdogan as well is a win,
max.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:38.490
Because look at the situation in his country,
look at how unhappy many Turks have been with

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:43.260
his leadership, there was a lot of speculation
that this

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.260
[8:03:27 AM]

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.780
a lot of speculation that this might be it,
this might be erdogan's last stand as many

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:48.260
has described it.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:54.080
But he has managed to emerge from this point
pretty much unscathed, despite the state of

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.339
the economy which is blamed on his policies.

00:09:57.339 --> 00:10:03.660
Despite the criticism that him and his government
got following that devastating earthquake,

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:11.050
with vhs asterisks initial rescue response
to that, the lack of preparedness.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:13.540
And still, look at these numbers.

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:16.240
He still has support of almost 50% of the
country.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.890
Max, what these results tell us

